WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.900
Anyone familiar with the hit series Lucifer
knows that it's chock-full of memorable moments

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.480
and scenes.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.930
From a crook who gets caught with his pants
down to a detective turned into a human smoothie,

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.460
keep watching to find out about these moments
and more!

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.720
Despite season one's darker tone, there is
still some solid humor to be found, with many

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.950
solid exchanges and insults.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:25.220
One of the more entertaining moments is a
glorious exchange between Lucifer and Chloe

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.570
in the show's inaugural episode.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:32.230
Lucifer's extended vacation on earth is interrupted
when a famous friend of his is killed in a

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.410
drive-by shooting.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.180
The subsequent police investigation lands
him in the crosshairs of Detective Chloe Decker,

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.430
with whom he tries to solve the murder.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:45.060
Their partnership is, at first, very one-sided
with Lucifer skirting various legalities to

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.329
interrogate people, including dangling a rapper
out of a window.

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:54.210
It's after this near act of homicide that
one of the rapper's entourage points out Chloe's

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.850
former life as an actor.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.600
Lucifer is quick to jump on this and praise
Chloe's assets in a movie titled "Hot Tub

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.600
High School."

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.460
"The one with the famous nude scene, coming
out of the hot tub!

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.140
It was like a complete "Fast Times" rip-off,
she was like the new Phoebe Cates!"

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.490
She quickly asserts her authority by slapping
cuffs on him for his actions, much to Lucifer's

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.270
sadistic delight.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:17.250
With the broader comedic set pieces of later
seasons, it's fun to look back on simpler

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.960
exchanges like this one.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.860
It's an early taste of the frequently recurring
dynamic that would make the devil and cop

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.740
duo so likable.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.860
We are first shown a taste of Lucifer's backstory
in season one when amidst an investigation

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.820
Chloe sees Lucifer's scars.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:35.070
"Now you can't argue with that, can you?"

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:40.300
It's a low-key but very effective moment where
Lucifer doesn't sugarcoat the actual truth,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.850
stating very bluntly that the scars are leftover
from where he cut off his wings in defiance

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:45.850
of his father.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.630
"Your father did that to you?"

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:48.630
"No!

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.990
That's where I cut my wings off.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.480
Well I didn't, Maze did.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.780
I told her to."

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.680
Chloe, not yet a believer in Lucifer's demonic
status, doesn't truly grasp the truth behind

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.680
his scars.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.799
She looks upon them with what appears to be
genuine shock and legitimate sympathy, and

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:07.320
she quickly stops when Lucifer asks her not
to touch them.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:12.029
The interactions between Lucifer and Amenadiel
are always a persistent source of drama throughout

00:02:12.029 --> 00:02:13.799
the entire series.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:18.319
Their often strained relationship would grow
from a heated rivalry rife with deceptions

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:21.099
to a healthy and mature familial bond.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:25.019
During the show's first season we would get
a taste of this kinder relationship in the

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:27.019
episode "Wingman."

00:02:27.019 --> 00:02:31.059
Lucifer's prized possession, his wings, had
been stolen and he'd made it his mission to

00:02:31.059 --> 00:02:32.659
get them back.

00:02:32.659 --> 00:02:37.329
After determining that a piece of divinity
let loose on earth would spell disaster, Amenadiel

00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:39.459
begrudgingly agrees to help.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:43.379
This leads them to an underground auction
where the wings are listed as a high-priced

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:46.700
item, amongst other alleged divine relics.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.849
During the bid for the first item, the chains
of St. Paul, the brothers would share a brief

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:52.439
moment of comradery.

00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:54.930
"Paul's wrists were too thick to fit in those
chains."

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:58.719
"I know, that man could never pass up on dessert."

00:02:58.719 --> 00:03:00.819
"He should have been the saint of…"

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:01.819
"Honey cakes!"

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:05.889
They not only point them out as fake but take
time to dunk on St. Paul's inability to pass

00:03:05.889 --> 00:03:10.819
on dessert, sharing a laugh before resuming
their respectively combative tones.

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:15.439
This is undercut later by the revelation that
Amedadiel played a role in the wing's theft.

00:03:15.439 --> 00:03:19.980
However, it's a legitimately sweet moment
and a precursor to the emotional growth both

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.430
characters would soon make.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:26.840
Father Frank was a one-shot character who
definitely left a major impact on Lucifer

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.639
and the show's fandom.

00:03:28.639 --> 00:03:33.230
In the Season 1 episode "A Priest Walks Into
a Bar," the streetwise priest comes to Lucifer

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.040
looking for a favor.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.629
He asks Lucifer to help him with Connor, an
orphaned youth who Frank saw fit to take under

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:40.629
his wing.

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:45.670
Lucifer, being repellent to anyone who serves
his father, is initially callous to Frank.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.559
This would change when Frank, under Lucifer
and Chloe's protection, shares his backstory

00:03:49.559 --> 00:03:51.549
as a traveling musician.

00:03:51.549 --> 00:03:55.730
Frank's life changed after a car accident
killed not only Connor's parents but Frank's

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.409
daughter as well.

00:03:57.409 --> 00:04:01.669
After this sobering revelation, Lucifer feels
intrigued by Frank's claim of being a superior

00:04:01.669 --> 00:04:04.499
piano player and demands to see him in action.

00:04:04.499 --> 00:04:09.919
The duo then engages in a competitive but
friendly piano duet and genuinely seems content

00:04:09.919 --> 00:04:11.079
in each other's company.

00:04:11.079 --> 00:04:12.079
"Oh!

00:04:12.079 --> 00:04:15.260
I think I know what you mean.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.830
Something like that?"

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:17.830
"Yeah!"

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:21.700
Chloe, upon returning, sees the two playing
together and smiles as she sees Lucifer actually

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.380
connecting with someone.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:27.260
This newfound friendship would be cut short
by Frank's untimely death, something that

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:30.170
Lucifer responds to with furious anger.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:34.690
Despite only making one onscreen appearance,
Frank plays a major role in Lucifer finding

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.540
his humanity and growing as a person.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.730
The Season 1 finale of Lucifer definitely
ends the show's story arc with a fittingly

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:42.810
large bang.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:47.530
Malcolm, a recently resurrected dirty cop,
looks to reclaim his money by holding Trixie,

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.540
Chloe's daughter, hostage.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:54.031
It's a situation made all the direr because
of Lucifer's newfound mortality, something

00:04:54.031 --> 00:04:56.690
Malcolm takes full advantage of.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.880
Lucifer attempts to draw on Malcolm's desires,
but the latter reveals that his true desire

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:03.150
is to see Lucifer die.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.630
With a bullet in his stomach, all seems lost
for the former ruler of hell until, in a moment

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.580
of desperation, he turns to someone unexpected:
God.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:16.410
Lucifer makes a plea to his father, that he'll
finally do his bidding if God protects Chloe.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:22.850
"All that I ask…is that you protect Chloe."

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:26.190
His father hears the message and restores
Lucifer to his full strength.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:30.530
It's a wonderfully directed moment, only enhanced
by Tom Ellis' performance.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:34.710
It may be a smaller-scale victory, especially
when compared to the larger multi-character

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:40.000
battles in future finales, but it serves as
the perfect bookend for Season 1 and sets

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.110
up intriguing plot developments for Season
2.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:47.360
Added to the cast in Season 2 is Lucifer's
mother who, after escaping hell, inhabits

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.180
the body of the recently deceased Charlotte
Richards.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:55.420
Upon arriving on Earth, "Charlotte" goes about
making things complicated for Lucifer and

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.360
Chloe, and their budding relationship.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.120
From nearly blowing up Chloe with a car bomb,
to almost blasting Linda with her celestial

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:06.220
energy, Charlotte's arrival is marked by rampant
insanity.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:10.290
One moment that shouldn't be forgotten is
a devious stunt she pulled on the perpetually

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.210
gullible Dan Espinoza.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:16.730
While leaning into her life as Charlotte Richards,
the goddess of creation begins a fling with

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:21.800
the hapless detective, which leads to a very
steamy public kiss in front of several restaurant

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:26.210
patrons, including Amenadiel, her other son.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.430
"Ugh!"

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:35.300
Amenadiel's sorrow is punctuated by a giddy
Maze taking pictures of his reaction.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.210
This moment, as well as their entire love
affair, would, of course, have repercussions

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.230
later on for Dan.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:45.120
Trixie may never get much to do on her own,
but she still has wonderful chemistry with

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.120
others.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:49.930
A sizable amount of Maze's character development
has a lot to do with her relationship with

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:54.750
Trixie, which is similar to that of what an
aunt might have with her niece.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:58.590
Many of the most riveting scenes of the show
have Trixie somewhere in the crosshairs of

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:00.360
that season's danger.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:05.120
Anytime we get to see Lucifer interact with
Trixie it is a guaranteed source of charm

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.220
and hilarity.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:10.890
From traumatizing her schoolyard bully with
his devil face to buying her a doll, Lucifer

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:13.900
has certainly given her an interesting childhood.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:19.580
The swear jar joke, though a remarkably simple
one, always elicits sizable laughs.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:23.930
Lucifer discovers that Trixie must put money
in a jar for Chloe every time she uses foul

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:24.930
language.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:25.930
"Swear jar?"

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:27.740
"Oh yes, it's Trixie's."

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.570
"You give your child money every time she
swears?!

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.920
Oh, bravo detective!"

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:38.550
In response to this revelation, Lucifer tries
to give her a crisp 20 dollar bill to spend

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.350
on ample curse words.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:44.670
Later on, Chloe reprimands him for teaching
Trixie "loophole" curse words to skirt around

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.240
the swear jar stipulation.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.300
"Well she called her math homework a cluster-duck,
and her teacher a mother flunker."

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:56.210
It's a hilarious moment and another key factor
in Lucifer's ever-growing appreciation for

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:57.620
humanity.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:01.260
It would take a long time before Maze would
finally find a partner that could match her

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:03.870
spontaneity and dubious morality.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.980
By the end of the final season, that partner
would reveal themself to be Eve, the first

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:08.980
woman.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:12.750
However, before Maze was chasing dangerous
bounties into the sunset with Eve, there was

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.280
a road not taken.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:19.400
In Season 3 she would seek a change of pace
to her now very cyclical work-life balance.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:24.530
In order to shake things up, she opts to chase
a bounty by the name of Ben Rivers to Canada.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:29.530
Ben quickly proves himself to be just as crafty
as Maze, making for a very playful chase between

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:30.530
them.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:34.889
Ben eventually explains that his status as
a serial killer is false and that he had been

00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:35.889
framed.

00:08:35.889 --> 00:08:39.680
Maze agrees to help him and, with the help
of her friends in Los Angeles, is able to

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.099
clear his name.

00:08:41.099 --> 00:08:44.690
Before he goes off into the night, Ben offers
Maze the opportunity to come with him.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.982
"What if you come with me?

00:08:45.982 --> 00:08:48.389
You and me, we're the same.

00:08:48.389 --> 00:08:52.670
No roots.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.139
No family."

00:08:56.139 --> 00:09:00.709
Maze considers it but ultimately chooses her
life in L.A. over a future with Ben.

00:09:00.709 --> 00:09:05.769
Their goodbye is definitely a meaningful moment,
but an important part of her growth.

00:09:05.769 --> 00:09:10.040
When Lucifer moved to Netflix for its fourth
year, series creators definitely took advantage

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.930
of their newfound lack of restrictions.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:17.249
After rekindling his relationship with the
free-spirited Eve, Lucifer's regained streak

00:09:17.249 --> 00:09:20.870
of debauchery leaks into his life at work.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:25.740
One notable moment inspired an episode title
after Lucifer wears his, quote, "Orgy Pants

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:26.839
To Work."

00:09:26.839 --> 00:09:31.249
For many, one glimpse of Lucifer's rear end
would be enough, but the episode saw fit to

00:09:31.249 --> 00:09:33.020
up the ante.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:37.110
While on the case of a recent victim, Chloe
and Lucifer's investigation leads them to

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:38.589
a nudist colony.

00:09:38.589 --> 00:09:43.959
In order to enter they must disrobe, a stipulation
that Chloe protests, but Lucifer and Ella

00:09:43.959 --> 00:09:45.930
quickly embrace with gusto.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:46.930
"Lucifer!"

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:48.769
"Oh, when in Rome detective."

00:09:48.769 --> 00:09:53.850
Season 4 is where the show really starts leaning
heavily into its comedic elements, and this

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.110
is a prime example of that shift.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:00.350
It's an underrated, yet hysterical little
moment that showcases the show's vibrant and

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:03.519
often madcap new creative direction.

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:08.519
If Lucifer fans were only allowed to make
a gif out of just one moment from the show,

00:10:08.519 --> 00:10:10.970
we'd like to make a case for this one.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:15.189
When the show's fifth season dropped, the
cast was joined by Statefarm spokesman Dennis

00:10:15.189 --> 00:10:18.180
Haysbert as Lucifer's dad, God himself.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:22.629
God, being all-knowing, already felt familiar
with the show's core characters, including

00:10:22.629 --> 00:10:23.829
poor Dan.

00:10:23.829 --> 00:10:28.439
Dan, upon realizing just who he is talking
to, starts behaving strangely, to humorous

00:10:28.439 --> 00:10:29.439
effect.

00:10:29.439 --> 00:10:30.439
"Hey.

00:10:30.439 --> 00:10:31.439
Mister, uh, God.

00:10:31.439 --> 00:10:36.120
Listen, um, I'm sorry that I slept with your
wife.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.129
I didn't know she was married at the time,
I swear to—"

00:10:39.129 --> 00:10:43.319
God at first seems very laid back about the
situation, but then quickly showcases his

00:10:43.319 --> 00:10:48.420
true feelings on the matter by exploding Dan
into a human smoothie that paints the walls,

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.279
much to Lucifer's shock.

00:10:50.279 --> 00:10:54.459
God very quickly reverses the event and puts
Dan back together, but leaves the poor detective

00:10:54.459 --> 00:10:56.519
frazzled and traumatized.

00:10:56.519 --> 00:11:01.200
A rare show of anger from God during his tenure
as a supporting character, but a morbid and

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.970
hilarious one.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:07.160
It's fair to say that Lucifer leaned heavily
into its comedic elements after the show switched

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.119
from FOX to Netflix.

00:11:09.119 --> 00:11:14.029
Gone was the darker noir aesthetic of the
early seasons, and in its place were comedy

00:11:14.029 --> 00:11:15.570
and bright colors.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:19.589
The show's final season definitely doubles
down on comedic moments, with one serving

00:11:19.589 --> 00:11:21.930
as its ultimate crescendo.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:25.899
With things amiss in heaven, Lucifer plans
to see what the problem is, but unfortunately,

00:11:25.899 --> 00:11:28.000
he can't get his wings to work.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.580
Lucifer also discovers that Linda has been
compiling all her data on him in order to

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.709
pen a tell-all book.

00:11:34.709 --> 00:11:38.470
The group decides to cull through this data
in order to pinpoint what's going on with

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:42.119
Lucifer's wings, and hilarity naturally ensues.

00:11:42.119 --> 00:11:47.410
The most gut-busting moment is Linda's very
direct interpretation of the gang's day-to-day

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:48.410
interactions.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:52.579
It's a sequence that feels like someone made
a bot watch every episode of the series, then

00:11:52.579 --> 00:11:53.670
write a script.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.350
"Crazy that the killer was the first person
we met!"

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:57.990
"What are the chances?"

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:58.990
"I know!"

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:04.459
It's a scene run totally on auto-pilot, with
every character's identifiable or quirky trait

00:12:04.459 --> 00:12:09.209
maxed out to eleven, complete with a comically
stock back-and-forth between Lucifer and Chole

00:12:09.209 --> 00:12:13.220
and Maze cartoonishly pulling a severed human
head out of a bag.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:17.559
It's a truly wonderful moment and a hilarious
summation of why fans love these characters

00:12:17.559 --> 00:12:19.250
so much.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:21.240
